content.text:
Now app.js. Need import:
```
import {W,H,SKINS,..., emptyLook, studioLook, presetLook, normalizeLook, PRESETS, CLIENTS, ROUND_TIME, skinOf...} from './data.js';
import {createFaceRenderer,isOnFace} from './face.js';
```
We need palettes for swatches: SKINS, HAIRS, EYES, BLUSHES, SHADOWS, LIPS, LINERS, BROWS, BRUSH_COLORS, AURAS, PRESETS, CLIENTS, ROUND_TIME, AURAS, emptyLook etc.
Also maybe getters for names.

DOM refs.

Canvas setup:
```
const paintCanvas=document.createElement('canvas');
const renderer=createFaceRenderer(canvas,paintCanvas);
```
`resize` on window resize? DPR change; add debounce call renderer.resize then render.
But CSS size resize doesn't affect dpr. devicePixelRatio may change; call occasionally. We'll add `window.addEventListener('resize', ()=>{ renderer.resize(); render(); })` but resizing canvas resets; okay. It could clear paint layer; render rebuilds. Good.

State:
```
let look = studioLook();
let history=[];
let mode='free';
let modalClosable=false;
const ui={ tab:'skin', sticker:'gem', brushColor:'#b04463', brushMode:'draw', brushSize:8, brushOpacity:80, muted:false};
const game={round:0,score:0,stars:[],timeLeft:ROUND_TIME,timerId:null,finished:false,presented:false};
```
Saved values load: muted, best.

`loadJSON(key)`.

On boot:
- look = normalizeLook(loadJSON(LOOK_KEY)) || studioLook(); Wait saved may be empty? If saved exists use it. `const saved=loadJSON(LOOK_KEY); if(saved) look=normalizeLook(saved);`
- ui.muted = !!loadJSON(MUTE_KEY)
- set sound btn class
- build UI swatches, presets, tabs events, etc.
- renderer.render(look)
- update best note
- syncUI
- start screen visible.
Maybe saved look shows behind start overlay—nice.

Need start screen hidden by default? HTML start visible, app visible. Good.

Functions:

`$ = id => document.getElementById(id)`.
Refs.

`buildSwatches()`:
```
const sets = {
 skin: SKINS.map(x=>({id:x.id, hex:x.base, name:x.name})),
 blush...
 hairColor: HAIRS.map...
 eyeColor: EYES.map(x=>({id:x.id,hex:x.base,name:x.name})),
 shadow: SHADOWS, lips: LIPS, linerColor: LINERS, browColor: BROWS, brushColor: BRUSH_COLORS.map((hex,i)=>({id:hex,hex,name:'Color '+...}))
};
document.querySelectorAll('[data-swatches]').forEach(container=>{
 const key=...; if key==='aura' build aura; else ...
});
```
Brush color swatches use dataset.id=hex and active compare ui.brushColor.
For IDs with # in dataset fine.
Set title/aria-label.

Aura swatches:
```
el.dataset.id = a.id;
el.style.setProperty('--c', `linear-gradient(160deg, ${a.top}, ${a.mid} 55%, ${a.bottom})`);
```
Css uses background:var(--c).

Swatch button type=button. use class 'swatch'.

`setActiveSwatch(type, id)` maybe in sync: map container key to value. For aura use aura-swatch.

Sync UI:
```
function syncUI(){
 // tabs
 document.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach...
 document.querySelectorAll('.tab-pane')...
 // mode
 if(mode==='challenge'){...} else {...}
 // swatches
 const values={skin:look.skin, blush:look.blushColor, shadow:look.shadowColor, lips:look.lips, hairColor:look.hairColor, eyeColor:look.eyeColor, linerColor:look.linerColor, browColor:look.browColor, brushColor:ui.brushColor, aura:look.aura};
 ...
 // segmented
 const segmentMap={shadowFinish:look.shadowFinish, liner:look.liner, lashes:look.lashes, brows:look.brows, lipFinish:look.lipFinish, hairstyle:look.hairstyle, earrings:look.earrings, necklace:look.necklace, brushMode:ui.brushMode};
 // toggles
 freckles/mole (two toggles moleToggle & moleToggle2) etc.
 // sliders values and labels
 setRange('blushRange', look.blushIntensity*100, 'blushVal', `${Math.round(...)}%`) ...
 // names
 shadowName, lipName, lipFinishName, linerName, browName, hairStyleName, brushModeName, brushSizeVal, brushOpacityVal
 // thumbs
 brushPreview.style.setProperty('--brush', ui.brushColor)
 // present label
 // undo disabled
 undoBtn.disabled = history.length===0
 // checklist update
 updateChecklist()
 // cursor, caption
 updateToolCursor()
 // dots/hud
}
```
Need update sliders' `--p` and labels. But setting range value while user drags might reset? same value. okay.

Mapping labels:
- shadowName = shadowOf(look).name
- lipName = lipOf(look).name
- lipFinishName capitalization map.
- linerName: none 'Sin delinear', soft 'Suave', wing 'Alas', bold 'Intenso'.
- browName: natural 'Naturales' etc.
- hairStyleName: loose 'Suelto', updo 'Recogido', bob 'Bob'.
- brushModeName: draw 'Trazo', glitter 'Glitter', erase 'Borrar'.

For slider fill: set `el.style.setProperty('--p', pct+'%')`.
`updateRange(id, value, valId, fmt)`.

History:
- `commit(fn)` push history; fn(look); afterLookChange.
- For slider: `beginRangeHistory` on pointerdown before change; but the same pointerdown on any range pushes; skip brush sliders. Implement listener on panel:
```
panelBody.addEventListener('pointerdown', e=>{
 const sl=e.target.closest('input[type=range]');
 if(sl && !['brushSize','brushOpacity'].includes(sl.dataset.slider)) pushHistory();
